  "gaps": [
    "2011: no annual verse-of-the-year or annual top-10 was published; only the cumulative all-time most-bookmarked infographic (June 2011) exists.",
    "2012: no 'Verse of the Year' designation existed yet; only the top-10 most-bookmarked list for 2012 (published Jan 2013).",
    "2015: no single global 'Verse of the Year' announcement found. YouVersion/Christianity Today reported Proverbs 3:5-6 as #1 most-shared of 2015 and Romans 12:2 as the all-time most popular; one search summary claimed Joshua 1:9 for 2015 but this could not be verified against any source and was excluded.",
    "2013 'Most Popular Verses' #3 is printed as Matthew 6:13 in YouVersion's own infographic; likely a typo for Matthew 6:33, recorded exactly as printed.",
    "Full 88-country table for 2016 and full 35-country table for 2017 exist; entries here group countries by verse per the Christianity Today table and the primary 2017 year-in-review page (2017 page grouped 23 additional countries under Joshua 1:9 / John 3:16 / Jeremiah 29:11 without individual attribution).",
    "2018-2025 announcements name only the single Verse of the Year (2025 adds two runner-up verses); no published global top-10 lists were found for those years.",
    "Some fetches blocked (churchleaders.com, eternitynews.com.au, christiantoday 2018 article returned 403); data for those years confirmed via alternate sources."
  ],
  "notes": "Verse of the Year by year: 2013 Philippians 4:13; 2014 Romans 12:2; 2016 Romans 8:28; 2017 Joshua 1:9; 2018 Isaiah 41:10; 2019 Philippians 4:6; 2020 Isaiah 41:10; 2021 Matthew 6:33; 2022 Isaiah 41:10; 2023 Isaiah 41:10; 2024 Philippians 4:6; 2025 Isaiah 41:10. 'Primary' = YouVersion blog, YouVersion newsroom, YouVersion's own year-in-review microsite, or official YouVersion press releases on GlobeNewswire/PRNewswire. 'News' = third-party coverage of YouVersion data (Christianity Today, Christian Post, Christian Today), including two official YouVersion infographics read directly from images (2011 bookmarking infographic from blog.youversion.com; 2013 year-in-review infographic as republished by Christian Post). Verse-of-the-year metric is consistently the combination of shares + bookmarks + highlights in the Bible App. Recurring dominant verses across all years: Isaiah 41:10 (6x #1), Philippians 4:6 (2x #1 as single verse, plus #1 bookmarked 2011/2012), Romans 12:2, Romans 8:28, Jeremiah 29:11, Joshua 1:9, Philippians 4:13, Matthew 6:33, Proverbs 3:5-6."
